    ("What is early (interceptive) orthodontic treatment?", "Interceptive — or phase one — treatment is carried out between roughly ages seven and ten. It uses appliances such as palatal expanders, space maintainers or partial braces to guide jaw growth and create room for permanent teeth, which can reduce the need for extractions or complex treatment later."),
